14.263 pip
==========

Piper TTS is an Open Source neural-net TTS engine.  This module exposes
Piper TTS to Emacs.

  1. Sandbox for <https://github.com/OHF-Voice/piper1-gpl>
  2. Install piper-tts in a virtual environment whose bin directory is
     on Emacs's PATH.
  3. Set location of voice data in ‘pip-data-dir’.  Default is
     ‘~/.local/share/voices-piper’
  4. Use that environment's Python to run ‘-m piper.download_voices’.
     Download a voice with its ‘--data-dir’ option set to
     ‘pip-data-dir’.
  5. ‘M-x pip-speak’ to speak.
  6. At present ‘piper’ is not suitable for use as a primary TTS engine
     for Emacsvox through this experimental per-request wrapper, given
     its model-load latency and fixed 22,050 Hz raw-output assumption.
  7. However it might be interesting to use it for lower-priority speech
     where quality trumps latency.

14.263.1 Pip Commands
---------------------

